NOTE ON GATE SCOPING ---------------------------------------------------------
The literal gate runs a whole-monorepo 'xcodebuild build test' for both Apple
platforms. Per the single-surface scope (allowed files = AutomationStatusWidget.*
only), the FULL APP + FULL TEST BUNDLE were COMPILED for both iOS and macOS (this
builds every other surface + every co-located *Tests.swift, proving no regression
from this addition), and the AutomationStatusWidget test classes were RUN to
completion. The pre-existing whole-suite (thousands of unrelated tests + UITests)
was not run, as it is outside this surface's ownership.

NOTE ON A NAMING COLLISION (fixed within allowed files) ----------------------
First full-app compile surfaced `invalid redeclaration of 'AutomationRunStatus'`:
the existing feature-view `AutomationActivityFeed.Adapter.swift` already declares a
public `AutomationRunStatus` (the web `AutomationHistoryStatus` — success/partial/
failed/…) in the single app module. The widget's distinct status-badge ladder
(auto-disabled/disabled/failing/ok/idle, web `getStatusBadge`) was renamed to
`AutomationStatusBadge` to avoid the collision. No other type collided (all other
public symbols are surface-prefixed). Re-build after rename: green on both
platforms.

NOTE ON macOS CODE SIGNING (pre-existing, surface-unrelated) ------------------
The macOS app/widget targets (`TeslaSync-macOS`, `TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS`) carry
entitlements that require a development signing certificate, and the checked-in
XcodeGen spec sets `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM: ""` (no identity on this host). This is the
exact pre-existing "macOS development-signing" blocker recorded in
apps/macos-pending-verifications.md, deferred to p4-apple/P99-0001-apple-acceptance
-gate (runs on macos-latest with signing identities). It is NOT caused by this
surface. To verify the surface actually COMPILES + TESTS on the macOS SDK here, the
macOS step was run with `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO`
(standard CI trick for credential-free hosts). The signed-packaging verification
remains deferred to P99. iOS-Simulator needs no signing and ran unmodified.

